---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Contact | SubFixer';
const description = 'Get in touch with the person behind SubFixer. Report a bug, ask a question, or suggest a feature.';
const path = '/contact/';
const jsonld = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'ContactPage',
    'name': 'Contact',
    'description': 'Get in touch with the person behind SubFixer. Report a bug, ask a question, or suggest a feature.',
    'url': 'https://subfixer.app/contact/'
  }
];
const ogType = 'website' as const;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} jsonld={jsonld} ogType={ogType}>
  <div class="guide">
    <h1>Contact</h1>
    <p class="lede">SubFixer is a one-person project. I built it because subtitle files kept breaking in ways that were tedious to fix by hand.</p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>Write to <a href="mailto:hello@subfixer.app">hello@subfixer.app</a>. I read every message and reply within a few days.</p>

    <h2>Bug reports</h2>
    <p>If something is not working, include these details so I can reproduce it:</p>
    <ul class="plainlist spaced">
      <li>Your browser and version (e.g., Chrome 130, Firefox 132, Safari 18)</li>
      <li>The input format (SRT, VTT, ASS, etc.) and the output format you chose</li>
      <li>A short sample of the subtitle file (10 to 20 lines) with any private text removed</li>
      <li>What you expected to happen and what happened instead</li>
    </ul>
    <p>A sample you choose to email is shared with us; files you open in the tools never leave your device.</p>

    <h2>Feature requests</h2>
    <p>If there is a format you need or a fix that would save you time, describe the problem you are trying to solve. The clearest requests come with a real example.</p>

    <h2>Other questions</h2>
    <p>Licensing, attribution, or anything else: just ask. The tool is free and runs entirely in your browser. The <a href="/about/">about page</a> says more about the project, and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> explains what the site collects.</p>
  </div>
</Base>